@startuml User_Stories_Sequence
title User Registration & Login Sequence - Authentication Flow

participant "Client" as CLIENT
participant "API Router" as ROUTER
participant "Rate Limiter" as RATE_LIMIT
participant "JWT Provider" as JWT
participant "Auth Service" as AUTH_SVC
participant "User Repository" as USER_REPO
participant "Database" as DB
participant "Email Service" as EMAIL_SVC

== Registration Flow ==
CLIENT -> ROUTER: POST /api/auth/register\n{email, password, name}
ROUTER -> RATE_LIMIT: Check Rate Limit
RATE_LIMIT -> ROUTER: OK - Limit Remaining: 99
ROUTER -> AUTH_SVC: register(RegisterRequest)
AUTH_SVC -> USER_REPO: findByEmail(email)
USER_REPO -> DB: SELECT * FROM users WHERE email=?
DB -> USER_REPO: No records found
USER_SVC -> AUTH_SVC: Email available ✓
AUTH_SVC -> AUTH_SVC: Validate Password (>= 8 chars)
AUTH_SVC -> USER_REPO: save(newUser)
USER_REPO -> DB: INSERT INTO users
DB -> USER_REPO: User ID: 123
USER_REPO -> AUTH_SVC: User Created
AUTH_SVC -> EMAIL_SVC: sendWelcomeEmail(email)
EMAIL_SVC -> EMAIL_SVC: Format Email Template
EMAIL_SVC -> CLIENT: Email Sent
CLIENT -> AUTH_SVC: Return Success + UserID
AUTH_SVC -> ROUTER: HTTP 201 Created
ROUTER -> CLIENT: {success: true, userId: 123, email}

== Login Flow ==
CLIENT -> ROUTER: POST /api/auth/login\n{email, password}
ROUTER -> RATE_LIMIT: Check Rate Limit (Standard API)
RATE_LIMIT -> ROUTER: OK - Employee Limit: 29/30
ROUTER -> AUTH_SVC: login(LoginRequest)
AUTH_SVC -> USER_REPO: findByEmail(email)
USER_REPO -> DB: SELECT * FROM users WHERE email=?
DB -> USER_REPO: {id: 123, role: ROLE_EMPLOYEE, ...}
USER_REPO -> AUTH_SVC: User Found
AUTH_SVC -> AUTH_SVC: Verify Password Hash
AUTH_SVC -> JWT: createAccessToken(email, role)
JWT -> JWT: Sign Token with Secret Key
JWT -> AUTH_SVC: eyJhbGc...PAYLOAD...SIGNATURE
AUTH_SVC -> JWT: generateRefreshToken(email)
JWT -> AUTH_SVC: eyJhbGc...(REFRESH)
AUTH_SVC -> ROUTER: {token, refreshToken, userId, role}
ROUTER -> CLIENT: HTTP 200 OK\n{accessToken, refreshToken}
CLIENT -> CLIENT: Store Token in LocalStorage

== Protected Request with Token ==
CLIENT -> ROUTER: GET /api/documents\nHeader: Authorization: Bearer [token]
ROUTER -> RATE_LIMIT: Check Rate Limit (Employee)
RATE_LIMIT -> ROUTER: OK - Limit: 28/30
ROUTER -> JWT: validateToken(token)
JWT -> JWT: Verify Signature & Expiration
JWT -> ROUTER: Valid ✓
ROUTER -> JWT: extractEmail(token)
JWT -> ROUTER: user@example.com
ROUTER -> JWT: extractRole(token)
JWT -> ROUTER: ROLE_EMPLOYEE
ROUTER -> AUTH_SVC: loadUserDetails(email)
AUTH_SVC -> USER_REPO: findByEmail(email)
USER_REPO -> DB: SELECT with Role
DB -> USER_REPO: User with ROLE_EMPLOYEE
AUTH_SVC -> ROUTER: CustomUserPrincipal(id, email, role)
ROUTER -> ROUTER: Set SecurityContext
ROUTER -> ROUTER: Route to Controller
ROUTER -> CLIENT: Response with User Data

== Rate Limit Exceeded ==
CLIENT -> ROUTER: GET /api/ai/chat\n(31st request in 1 min)
ROUTER -> RATE_LIMIT: Check AI Chat Rate Limit
RATE_LIMIT -> RATE_LIMIT: Employee Limit: 5/min
RATE_LIMIT -> RATE_LIMIT: Current: 5 consumed
RATE_LIMIT -> ROUTER: LIMIT EXCEEDED ❌
ROUTER -> CLIENT: HTTP 429 Too Many Requests\n{error: "Too many requests..."}

@enduml
